#
# Per-arm decode step mean, peak host RAM, and trajectory structure:
#   01-off                        8.165 ms  peak_ram_gb=21.925  distinct=3 cycle=3
#   02-on                         8.335 ms  peak_ram_gb=21.924  distinct=3 cycle=3
#   03-pairwise                   8.199 ms  peak_ram_gb=21.931  distinct=3 cycle=3
#   04-on-fault-prefetch_stale    8.234 ms  peak_ram_gb=21.924  distinct=3 cycle=3  NULL
#   05-on-fault-prefetch_zero     8.286 ms  peak_ram_gb=21.924  first_diff=0        DETECTED
#   06-pairwise-fault-plane_byte  8.219 ms  peak_ram_gb=22.845  distinct=3 cycle=3  NULL
#   07-pairwise-fault-plane_shift 8.281 ms  peak_ram_gb=22.847  first_diff=0        DETECTED
#
# Bootstrap result (the reason run #3 exists): feeding token 7020 instead of the
# golden continuation did NOT open the trajectory. The guards emit
# 509, 902, 7020, 509, 902, 7020, ... - a DIFFERENT period-3 attractor from
# runs #1/#2. The public long-copy gate makes the model emit 509, 902, then
# repeat whatever token it was last given, so every self-fed trajectory on this
# fixture is a period-3 attractor seeded by the bootstrap token. Free-run
# compounding is therefore unreachable on this fixture by seed choice alone.
# What run #3 did buy: both positive controls now diverge at step 0 (so the
# detector has demonstrated step-0 power), and plane_byte finally produced a
# clean rc=0 measurement whose 22.845 GB peak-RAM signature shows the halved-
# plane branch executed.
#
# Honest reading: prefetch_stale's null across all three batteries is a
# MAGNITUDE result (3 of 4 K-blocks of every gate/up row read a neighbouring
# group's E4M3 scale and no argmax moved), not evidence of a dead hook - the
# hook is proven live by prefetch_zero on the same build. Mechanism (a)'s
# bit-exactness therefore remains BRACKETED, not closed.
#
# Reproduce:
#   OUT=/tmp/maple-shared-qmv-freerun3 MODE=freerun STEPS=256 BOOTSTRAP=7020 \
#     bash research/maple_shared_qmv_fault_injection.sh
#
